      "textEn": "120\n\nIs not. Therefore, to attain this knowledge, Brahma and other gods respectfully bowed to God.\nThey did. The feet are his own creation,\nWhere the fourfold is the creator. That great being, the self-manifested one,\nIs pleased by the great glory of Brahman. 32. Meaning of the word\n\nPadau—the lotus feet of his feet; Mahi—Earth; Iyam—This; Swa-krita—produced by oneself; Eva—indeed; Yasya—whose;\nChatuh-vidha—of four types of beings; Yatra—where; Hi—indeed; Bhuta-sargah—the material creation; Saha—He; Vai—indeed;\nMaha-purushah—the supreme being; Atma-tantrah—self-dependent, self-contented; Prasidatam—May we be gracious to them; Brahma—the greatest; Maha-\nVibhuti—Endowed with immense power. On this earth, there are four types of living beings, and all of them were produced by them. This physical creation stands on the lotus feet of him. They are supreme beings full of splendor and power. May Heavenly Father be pleased with us.\nMeaning: The word 'Mahi' is indicative of the five physical elements—Earth, Water, Air, Fire, and Space—which are dependent on the lotus feet of God. The greatness of merit is the virtuous glory of Murari. The great essence, that is, the entire physical\npower, rests on the lotus feet of God because this vast world is another glory of God.\nIs. In this vast world, there are four types of organisms—jarayaj (born from the embryo), andandaj (born from the eggs), swedaj (born from the sweat), and udbhijj (born from the seeds). As confirmed by the Vedanta Sutra,\neverything originates from God. No one is independent, but\nGod is completely independent. Born of the first, knowing the other from the other, the master of the sounds. The meaning of the word Swarat is\n“Independent.” We are independent, but God is completely independent. Therefore, God is greater than all. Up to here,\nthat even Brahma, who created the vast universe, is merely another glory of God.\nPhysical\ncreation is made active by God, therefore God is not 