      "textEn": "124\n\nPrajnjire khama purushasya nabhyaha. The one who is in the body, with the senses,\nMay he be pleased, O great glory. 3. Meaning of the word\n\nFrom the ears; directions; from whom; from the heart; also; piercing; of the body; Prajnajire—\nproduced; Kham—sky; of the Supreme Being; Nabhyah—from the navel; Prana—of the life force; Indriya—organs;\nAtma—mind; Asu—life; body—and body; Ketu—causing; Praise—pleasure; Namah—to us; Sah—He; Maha-\nVibhuti—the supremely mighty. May the almighty Lord be pleased with us. Different directions originate from their ears,\nThe body's pores emerge from their heart, and the life force, senses, mind, the air within the body, and\nthe body's shelter-like void (sky) emerges from their navel. Balamhendra, the thirty-six, by grace,\nThe auspicious, the mountain, the fierce, the lord of the serpents.\nWho is the one who is pleased with the Khemyastuchhandasu yushayo medhataha\nWho is the one who is pleased with the great glory. 39. By force—by their strength; Maha-Indra—the king Indra could become; Trida-shah—and the gods; Prasadat—by being pleased; Manyoah—by anger;\nGiri-Ishah—Shiva; Dhishanaat—with deep intellect; Virinchah—Brahma; Khebhyah—from the physical openings; Tu—and; Chhandansi—\nVedic mantras; Rishayah—great sages; Medhatah—from the genitals; Kah—Prajapati-gana; Prasidatam—be pleased; Nah—to us;\nSah—He; Maha-Vibhuti—the supreme powerful Lord..\n\nThe king of heaven, Mahendra, was born from the power of God, the gods were born from the grace of God,\nwere born, Shivji was born from the anger of God, and Brahmaji was born from his profound intellect.\nWere born. All the Vedic mantras originated from the orifices of the body of God, and the sages and\nPrajapatis originated from their genitals. May the almighty God have mercy on us! Shri Rakshasa, under the shadow of his ancestors,\nDharma, from the breasts, emerged on the back.\nBy the play of the gods, the nymphs, and the apsaras,\nMay we be pleased, O great glory. 40. Meaning of the word\n\nShrih - Goddess of wealth; Vakshasah - from their chest; Pitarah - inhabitants of the mortal world; Chhayaah - from their shadow; Asan - a forest;\nSake; Dharmah - the principle of dharma; Stanat - from their breasts; Itharah - adharma (the opposite of dharma); Pishtah - from the back; Abhut - possible;\nHo Sakya; Dyuh - the heavens; Yasya - of whom; Shirnah - from the braid; Apsarah - inhabitants of the apsara realm; Viharah - their\nFrom the enjoyment of the senses; Prasidatam - be pleased; Nah - to us; Sah - He (God); Maha-vibhutih - the greatest in all valor.Lakshmi originated from their chest, the inhabitants of the father's world were from their shadow, dharma was from their breast"
